<figure class="auth-flow" aria-labelledby="auth-flow-title" aria-describedby="auth-flow-description">
  <div class="auth-flow__heading">
    <figcaption id="auth-flow-title">One request, two gateway decisions, two identities</figcaption>
    <p id="auth-flow-description">
      Follow the request from top to bottom. You use a Keycloak token at the gateway; the backend uses its ServiceAccount to call the OpenShift API.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="auth-flow__legend" aria-label="Identity legend">
    <span><i class="auth-flow__key auth-flow__key--human" aria-hidden="true"></i>Human identity: Keycloak JWT</span>
    <span><i class="auth-flow__key auth-flow__key--workload" aria-hidden="true"></i>Workload identity: <code>mcp-viewer</code></span>
  </div>

  <ol class="auth-flow__steps">
    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--human">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">1</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner">Keycloak</span>
        <strong>Issue a signed access token</strong>
        <p>The reader token contains <code>tool:pods_list_in_namespace</code>; the no-tools token does not.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--human">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">2</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner">MCP client</span>
        <strong>Send the request and token</strong>
        <p><code>POST /mcp</code> with <code>Authorization: Bearer …</code></p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--gate">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">3</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner"><code>mcp</code> listener · authentication gate</span>
        <strong>Authorino validates the token</strong>
        <p>Signature, issuer, and expiration must be valid.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="auth-flow__reject"><b>Fail</b> → HTTP 401</span>
    </li>

    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--router">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">4</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner">MCP broker and router</span>
        <strong>Resolve the backend and tool</strong>
        <p>The router supplies <code>mcp-exp/mcp-server-test</code> and <code>pods_list_in_namespace</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--gate">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">5</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner"><code>mcps</code> listener · authorization gate</span>
        <strong>Authorino compares the request with the token role</strong>
        <p>The required role is <code>tool:pods_list_in_namespace</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="auth-flow__reject"><b>Missing role</b> → HTTP 403</span>
    </li>

    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--workload">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">6</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner">OpenShift MCP server</span>
        <strong>Use the Pod's own cluster identity</strong>
        <p>In this lab, <code>kubeconfig</code> mode uses the backend's configured identity: <code>ServiceAccount/mcp-viewer</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="auth-flow__step auth-flow__step--workload">
      <span class="auth-flow__number">7</span>
      <div>
        <span class="auth-flow__owner">OpenShift API</span>
        <strong>Apply Kubernetes RBAC and return Pod data</strong>
        <p>You grant OpenShift permissions to <code>mcp-viewer</code> through RBAC.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="auth-flow__boundary">
    <section>
      <span>Gateway boundary</span>
      <strong>Keycloak JWT</strong>
      <p>Who is calling, and which MCP tool role do they have?</p>
    </section>
    <span class="auth-flow__separate" aria-label="is separate from">Separate identities</span>
    <section>
      <span>OpenShift API boundary</span>
      <strong><code>ServiceAccount/mcp-viewer</code></strong>
      <p>Which Kubernetes resources may the backend workload read?</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</figure>

